%% Figure 8 — Notification and Email Outbox Processing
flowchart LR
  Business[Bug or access action transaction] --> Write[Write notification source record\nand domain-specific delivery row]
  Write --> Email{Email required and\nprovider configuration ready?}
  Email -- No --> Skipped[(Delivery = SKIPPED\nor no delivery row)]
  Email -- Yes --> Pending[(Delivery = PENDING)]
  Skipped --> Commit{Business transaction\ncommitted?}
  Pending --> Commit
  Commit -- No --> Rollback[Rollback notification\nand delivery records]
  Commit -- Yes --> PendingCheck{Pending delivery\nexists?}
  PendingCheck -- No --> Complete([Delivery handling complete])
  PendingCheck -- Yes --> Immediate[Post-commit immediate\noutbox kick]
  PendingCheck -- Yes --> Scheduler[SAP Job Scheduling Service\nRecovery, retry and digest]
  Immediate --> Processor[Protected CAP\nprocessEmailOutbox]
  Scheduler --> Processor
  Processor --> Batch[Process Bug, invitation, access\nand digest delivery queues]
  Batch --> Eligible{Eligible by status, attempt,\nnext-attempt time and lock expiry?}
  Eligible -- No --> Leave[Leave row for a later run]
  Eligible -- Yes --> Claim[Conditionally claim row\nwith lock token and lease]
  Claim --> Send[Send allowlisted message\nthrough configured provider]
  Send --> Accepted{Provider accepted?}
  Accepted -- Yes --> Sent[(Delivery = SENT\nClear lock and errors)]
  Accepted -- No --> Failed[(Delivery = FAILED\nStore sanitized error)]
  Failed --> Retry{Attempts remain?}
  Retry -- Yes --> Backoff[Set bounded nextAttemptAt]
  Backoff --> Scheduler
  Retry -- No --> Final([Final failed delivery\nBusiness action remains committed])
  Sent --> Complete

